  "raw_text": "185\n\nPihtu\n \n(\nbc,dict,dictu\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \npineapple\n \n/ piña\n\nPihwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto go white, to become white, to grow white, to whiten, to become pale, to grow old (dict)\n \n/ ponerse\nblanco, volverse blanco, blanquearse, ponerse pálido, envejecer (\ndict\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Jan 4:35\n):\n \nNamkra nani buki insla nani ba ra kaiks, m\nâ\n \nba pat pihwan sa\n \n–\n \nRaising your eyes to the fields look, the grain is\nalready grown white\n \n/ Levantando la vista hacia los campos, el grano ya está blanco)\n\nPikak\n \n(\ndb,dictu\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \npeacock\n \n/ pavo real\n\nPikpik\n \n(\nPik pik\n-\nlfb\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nfrog\n \n/ rana\n\nPilala\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsoup, broth\n \n/ sopa, caldo\n\nPilimon\n \n(\ndb\n;\n \nPailimon\n-dba;\n \nFailimonra\n-dbta,lrw\n)\n \n–\n \nPhilemon\n \n(Bible book) / Filemón (libro bíblico)\n\nPilipai\n \n(\ndb,dba\n;\n \nFilipai Nanira\n-dbta,lrw\n)\n \n–\n \nPhilippians\n \n(Bible book) / Filipenses (libro bíblico)\n\nPinkitu\n \n(\ndictu\n;\n \nChinkinto\n-bc\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ncarao\n \n/ carao\n\n(\nNote/Nota\n: Creole\n/Criollo\n \n–\n \nstinkintoe)\n\nPint\n \n(a/t:\n \nPent\n-\ndictu\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \npaint\n \n/ pintura\n\nPint dingkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto paint, to apply paint\n \n/ pintar, aplicar pintura\n\nPint munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto paint, to draw\n \n/ pintar, dibujar\n\nPipti\n \n(\nmba-\n \nfrom English / de inglés)\n \n–\n \nfifty\n \n/ cincuenta\n\nPiptin\n \n(\nmba-\n \nfrom English / de inglés)\n \n–\n \nfifteen\n \n/ quince\n\nPirit\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nSpirit\n\nPirwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto stagger, to wobble, to falter, to teeter, to sway\n \n/ tambalearse, balancearse\n\n(Note/Nota: At\n \ndb\n-\nWihta nani 5:27\n,\n \nTirwi\n \nappears to be a spelling error of\n \nPirwi\n. / En db\n-\nWihta nani 5:27,\n \nTirwi\n \nparece ser un error\n\nortográfico de\n \nPirwi\n.)\n\nPirwi taukaia\n \n(\ndb-Hibru Nani 11:38\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto wander\n \n/ vagar\n\nPirwras\n \n(v-neg)\n \n–\n \nnot stagger, not wobble, not falter, not teeter, not sway\n \n/ no tambalearse, no vacilar, no\nbalancearse\n\nPîs\n \n(Pis)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npiece, section\n \n/ pieza, sección\n\n(Construct:\n \nPîska\n)\n\nBrit pîs\n \n–\n \npiece of bread\n \n/ pedazo de pan\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb48\n):\n \nPliskam pali, brit pîs kum aik\n \n–\n \nPlease give me a piece of bread\n \n/ Por favor dame un pedazo de pan)\n\nPîs pîs\n \n(Pis pis)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npieces\n \n/ piezas\n\nPîs pîs aisanka nani\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsymposium\n \n/ serie de discursos\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nY\nu\n \nkumi aidrubanka tara programka 2024\n-\n2025\n):\n \nPîs pîs aisanka nani:\n \nYang swiri ai daukras sa…\n \n–\n\nSymposium:\n \nI\n \nam\n \nn\not\n \na\nshamed of\n \n…\n \n/\n \nSerie de discursos:\n \nNo\n \nestoy\n \navergonza\nd\no...\n)\n\nPît\n \n(Pit)\n \n–\n \nfoot, feet\n \n(measurement) / pie, pies (medida)\n\nPit\n \n–\n \nfit, fitting, precise, precisely, point of, appropriate\n \n/ ajuste, preciso, punto de, apropiado\n\n(Construct:\n \nPitki, Pitkam, Pitka\n)\n\nPitka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npoint, the point of, extent, precise point, appropriate point\n \n/ punto, el punto de, límite, punto\npreciso, punto apropiado\n\n(\nEx/Ej(\nbh71\n):\n \nDia pitka kat upla pruan bukaia Jehovah brinka sa ki?\n \n–\n \nTo what point/extent is Jehovah desiring to raise the\ndead?\n \n/ ¿Hasta qué punto/grado desea Jehová resucitar a los muertos?)\n\nPitka mangkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto put at the appropriate point, to put a limit, to balance\n \n/ poner en el punto\napropiado, poner un límite, equilibrar\n\nPitka kat\n \n(adv)\n \n–\n \nto the appropriate point/degree/extent/limit, to the precise point/degree/extent/limit\n \n/ al\npunto/grado/límite apropiado, al punto/grado/límite preciso\n\n(\nEx/Ej(\nwqu-12/19\n):\n \nMark 6:30-34 nahki marikisa Jisas ba pitka kat wark takan bara ris brin?\n \n–\n \nHow does Mark 6:30-34\nshow that Jesus worked and rested to the appropriate extent?\n \n/ ¿Cómo muestra Marcos 6:30-34 que Jesús trabajó y\ndescansó en la medida apropiada?)\n\n(\nEx/Ej(\nmwb-02/20\n):\n \nLawana kum wan smalkisa celular ba pitka kat yawan yus munaia\n \n–\n \nOne song teaches us to use the\ncell phone appropriately\n \n/ Una canción nos enseña a usar el teléfono celular apropiadamente)\n\n(\nEx/Ej(\nmwb-09/20\n):\n \nDîa pitka kat G\nȃ\nd ba yawan kumi bani ra main wan kaikisa?\n \n–\n \nTo what extent does God pay attention\nto us as indivituals?\n \n/ Hasta qué grado está Dios pendiente de cada uno de nosotros (individualmente)?)\n\nPitka kat daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto do in an appropriate way, to do in a balanced way\n \n/ hacer de manera\napropiada, hacer de manera equilibrada",
